  "sections": {
    "actors": {
      "text": "1. Large Multinational Enterprises: Gain leverage through rapid conformity adaptation and scale advantages in absorption of compliance costs.\n2. Mid-Sized Exporters: Experience relative leverage loss due to limited regulatory lobbying power and risk of bearing downstream compliance indemnities.\n3. Regulatory & Standards Authorities: Gain heightened jurisdictional leverage as the gatekeepers of conformity recognition.\n4. Tier-1 Transatlantic Customers: Hold increased procurement leverage, enabling them to demand price concessions or proof of compliance readiness before legal enactment.",
