      "benefit": "Positions the exporter as a first mover among mid-market competitors if draft standards are enacted without alteration.",
      "downside": "High risk of stranded capital and wasted compliance work if final legal text renegotiates technical standards or rules of origin.",
      "conditions": "Only advisable if bilateral negotiators freeze technical Annexes and commit to a fixed timeline.",
      "basis_claim_ids": [
        "claim_large_vs_sme_compliance",
        "claim_ratification_uncertainty"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "indicators": [
    {
      "indicator_id": "ind_final_rules_of_origin",
      "indicator": "Publication of finalized legal text specifying rules of origin and conformity assessment protocols",
      "trigger": "Official release of signed legal treaty text by US and EU trade authorities",
      "posture_change": "Transition from provisional contract clauses to executing binding long-term supply agreements and formal certification filings.",
      "basis_claim_ids": [
        "claim_user_summary_scope",
        "claim_ratification_uncertainty"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "key_unknowns": [
    "Exact binding legal definitions and phase-in schedules for conformity assessment recognition.",
    "Specific sector exemptions or carve-outs that may be introduced during final legislative ratification.",
    "Dispute settlement mechanisms and speed of resolution for mid-sized commercial entities."
